://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107638#issuecomment-2984440887","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107638","id":2984440887,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6x4vQ3","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-18T14:26:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-18T14:26:05Z","body":"Well it is important to use the functionality as it is intended, instead you should probably update the target only when it's moved far away enough from the previous position, that's probably what other engines do for that kind of functionality anyway\n\nBut to confirm: This problem goes away when the `target_position` isn't updated too often?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2984440887/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2984914019","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107638#issuecomment-2984914019","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107638","id":2984914019,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6x6ixj","user":{"login":"EricDeng1001","id":28720903,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NzIwOTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28720903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001","html_url":"https://github.com/EricDeng1001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-18T16:24:18Z","updated_at":"2025-06-18T16:24:18Z","body":"Good idea! I will try to implement it and try. I will report the result asap","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2984914019/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2985157174","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107638#issuecomment-2985157174","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107638","id":2985157174,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6x7eI2","user":{"login":"EricDeng1001","id":28720903,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NzIwOTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28720903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001","html_url":"https://github.com/EricDeng1001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-18T17:36:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-18T17:36:34Z","body":"OK, here is result. Only updating `target_position` when target is moved far enough do solve jitter problem when target is not moving too quickly or too often, but as soon as target itself is moving fast/frequently, jitter comes.\nOf course it does, because in that case we are updating `target_position` very often. But it is a COMMON CASE for game.\nMy experience in UE5 is totally different, which is very smooth and fast-response when following player. (by fast-response I mean, I don't need to calc distance moved from last path, and nav agent still follows my target closely)\nSo here is my thought: the root cause is still the inconsistency of the underlying navigation system.\n1. How often is needed to updated path is determined by the game, and we better not trade-off anything for that. \n2. If nav agent is at same point requesting same target position, requesting a path should generate stable result, rather than back-and-forth. This is very natural.\n3. I notice, even if I request a path each frame, when walking on plane, walking up slope, it's all working fine. Only walking down slope is problematic. I think this is understandable, because on slope, re-path always give a point slightly upper, so moving up is smooth, while moving down is back-and-forth","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2985157174/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2985239557","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107638#issuecomment-2985239557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107638","id":2985239557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6x7yQF","user":{"login":"EricDeng1001","id":28720903,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NzIwOTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28720903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001","html_url":"https://github.com/EricDeng1001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-18T18:03:20Z","updated_at":"2025-06-18T18:08:03Z","body":"More info: Using debug option of NavigationAgent3D to draw the path, I noticed that even when back-and-forth, the first point of path is not the same. It always slightly behind the agent (lets call it point A), and agent move towards it, and then, it give a point in front of agent, then agent move towards it, then navigation system again give a point behind the agent, (so, back-and-forth) (lets call it point B), but A != B. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2985239557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3493072525","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107638#issuecomment-3493072525","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107638","id":3493072525,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QNA6N","user":{"login":"EricDeng1001","id":28720903,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NzIwOTAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28720903?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001","html_url":"https://github.com/EricDeng1001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricDeng1001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-05T19:56:46Z","updated_at":"2025-11-05